{title: Keep Up Your Courage}
{subtitle: Acts 27:20–25; 27:41–44}
{key: Dm}
{tempo: 105}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [–] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] |
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [Dm] | [F] [C] | ×4
| [Dm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Dm]No sun, no stars for many days
Keep [F]up your [C]courage, [Dm]men
The storm was raging on the waves
Keep [F]up your [C]courage, [Dm]men
We gave up hope of being saved
Keep [F]up your [C]courage, [Dm]men
Then Paul stood up and spoke to us
Keep [F]up your [C]courage, [Dm]men
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
An [Bb]angel stood be[F]side me in the [C]night
Not [Dm]one of [C]you will be [Bb]lost
Only the ship, [F]only the [C]ship
Not [Dm]one of [C]you will be [Bb]lost
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Bb] | [Bb] |
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [F] [C] | [Dm] | ×2

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Dm]We struck a sandbar in the bay
Keep [F]up your [C]courage, [Dm]men
The stern was broken by the waves
Keep [F]up your [C]courage, [Dm]men
Some swam and some on planks of wood
Keep [F]up your [C]courage, [Dm]men
And every soul came safe to land
Keep [F]up your [C]courage, [Dm]men
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Bb] | [Bb] |
| [Dm] | [Dm] | [F] [C] | [Dm] | ×4
| [Dm] | [Dm] |
